+/* Two guards, one rule: the error card wants the same air (it keeps the flow berth and is the
+   assertive voice), and the crest takes the strip away whole. */
+.margin-note-previous.is-hidden,
+.margin-note-block.is-quiet .margin-note-previous {
+  display: none;
+}
+
+/* In-flow strip (<1024): an absolutely-positioned host inside the block, gapless, one line
+   box. In FLOW a second line costs 27.19px and the phone's centred column pays half of it —
+   the board rises 13.59px. Out of flow the board is invariant at every depth and the column
+   clears the ribbon by 4.80px on every phone rig measured. */
+@media (max-width: 1023.98px) {
+  .margin-note-block {
+    position: relative;
+  }
+
+  /* The voice takes the BLOCK's reserve, spoken or not, where it stands alone in the flow. The
+     push reads line one's rect as its `from`, and an empty voice here was a 0×0 box: any writer
+     that empties line one before pushing (AGE, ARM C's step) flew the record in from nowhere
+     (translate −34.17 scale 1.31, pass-3 critique). `inherit`, not a second number: the voice's
+     own line box is taller than the block's reserve on the landscape phones and grew the empty
+     strip there (+1.29 / +1.18px, docH +1 — F-ERASE-1's figure, the owner's), so the voice
+     follows whatever the block reserves. At ≥1024 the empty voice shares a baseline row with
+     line two, its bottom IS that baseline, and any reserve grows the strip (5.27px, pass 5). */
+  .margin-note {
+    min-height: inherit;
+  }
+
+  .margin-note-previous {
+    position: absolute;
+    top: 100%;
+    left: 0;
+  }
+}
+
+/* THE BALLOT, FIRED ON ITS OWN NUMBER (§2.3, landscape below 1024). The rule was: take the
+   trailing berth if the strip holds the two longest strings plus the gap, else depth one on
+   that pose. Measured on this build at 900×500: the strip is 332px and the pair needs 457.52px,
+   so it does not fit — and below the note that pose has 0px of air, where a second line puts
+   5.56px of the document past the fold (scrollHeight 500 → 506, chromium and webkit). Depth ONE
+   here, and it is a pose-dependent depth: B6's split-grammar row applies and the owner disposes
+   at the re-look. Stated, never hidden.
+
+   Depth one is the SIGHTED depth. `display: none` also took the record out of the reading
+   order, and the paragraph above line two says a reader can still reach it in browse mode; so
+   the line is clipped to nothing instead (the quiet voice's own pattern), seated on the block's
+   top edge so its one pixel adds no scroll. */
+@media (max-width: 1023.98px) and (orientation: landscape) {
+  .margin-note-previous {
+    top: 0;
+    width: 1px;
+    height: 1px;
+    overflow: hidden;
+    clip-path: inset(50%);
+  }
+}
+
+/* Overlay strip (≥1024): the TALLY'S berth (T4-P1 mark 6) — the verdict speaks, the older
+   line trails it in the quiet ink, one line for both. Below the note the desk has 5.55px of
+   air and a second line pushes the document 18.06px past the fold; beside it the two longest
+   strings fit the strip with zero scroll. The host must NOT take `position` here: the ≥1024
+   strip is already absolute, and an absolute line two inside it moves the desk's board.
+
+   `has-previous { flex-wrap: nowrap }` DIED in pass 2. It reversed T4-P1 mark 6 (which gave
+   the tally the right to a second line when it needs one) and bought nothing: the block is
+   48px tall either way, and nowrap only squeezed the tally into a wrap of its own and pushed
+   line two's ink 6.53px outside its box. `flex-basis: 0` is the honest answer — a hypothetical
+   main size of zero means line two never causes the wrap, the block keeps `wrap` for the
+   tally, and ink that will not fit is elided INSIDE the box (U+2026 is in the hand's cut).
+
+   AND NO `min-width` EVER, at either berth. A readable floor written as CSS is the wrap back:
+   this strip is `position: absolute; z-index: 50` and OVERLAYS, so a second row at 1024 lands
+   9.28px inside `button.ctrl-btn` — a tape over an interactive element, W2 §2.5's class law,
+   bought to keep an aged line legible. The floor is a GATE instead (L14): the used width is
+   measured against 12 × the element's own `1ch` at 1024 and 1280 with the block one row tall,
+   and it reds when the layout stops affording it rather than forcing the layout to. */
+@media (min-width: 1024px) {
+  .margin-note-previous {
+    flex: 1 1 0;
+    min-width: 0;
+    max-width: none;
+  }
 }
 
